Or:  When nurse dancing, make sure the first thing you do before taking
off your clothes is engrave "E" or drop a scroll of scare monster.
Then lure the nurse over. THEN take off your armor and weapon but NOT
your amulet of reflection.

Most monsters can't hit you but she can. This will give you enough time
to put on your clothes.  If things get critical,  have something like a
scroll of teleportation or a wand of digging in your main inventory.
Then either 'port away or go through the floor to get away.  THEN put
on your armor.

For me, the biggest danger in nurse dancing is not being hit by other
monsters but the temptation to simply lash out at a passing cockatrice,
forgetting that I'm not wearing gloves.

There's an art to nurse dancing. It can be done but it takes proper
preparation, time, and materials.  Even then it's not totally, 100%
safe.  But I've gained more than a hundred hit points from successful
nurse dancing.  To my mind,  the risk from adequately prepared nurse
dancing is less than the risk of traveling to Astral with limited hit
points.  But to each their own. 

